  "details": "Many incredible creations never make it to Quest—not because the avatars or worlds are poorly optimized, but because of the strict upload size limits. The current 100 MB cap for worlds and 10 MB limit for Quest avatars are a major bottleneck.\n\nWith so many experienced creators who do understand proper optimization—especially those participating in the Creator Economy—it would be a huge benefit if Quest upload size limits could be expanded for verified Creator Economy members.\n\nThis would reward creators who consistently produce high-quality, optimized content, while still maintaining overall performance and platform standards. Even a moderate size increase would allow more ambitious, well-made content to reach Quest users.\n\nWhether this involves creating a separate Community Labs section or another system entirely, it’s worth seriously considering.",
